  "preserved_facts": [
    "Greeting, farewell and mineral-delivery prefixes and suffixes retain dynamic player-name insertion. Cached starbas.c uses pStr + optional SPACE/GLOBAL_PLAYER_NAME when !usingSpeech + tail; name-present and omitted concatenations checked, not runtime.",
    "Ready-base and crew descriptions preserve dynamic ship names, five-unit warp cost, 50-person pods, 50-unit fuel tanks, firing arcs, limited staffing and possible RU increase.",
    "Resource acquisition, mining advice and original English color mnemonic retained; historical chronology, uncertainty and Hayes limited knowledge not replaced with later revelations.",
    "Alliance blueprints and captains, three Arilou ships, Melnorme rendezvous, Spathi disappearance, 100:50 disturbance and probe warning retained.",
    "Chmmr modification takes two weeks; escape unit removed, ten rear slots occupied and six remaining, resource provision unchanged.",
    "Crew-sale rumors, evidence, anger, increased recruitment cost and promised prosecution remain separate variants.",
    "Scientist reports use report register. Talking Pet mind-control interruption remains unexplained; bomb 12 AU warning, Sun Device 1/100 of 1% and sixteen Shofixti females retained.",
    "All 300 base records now reviewed against installed source; the final 125 IDs include scientist device reports, conditional advice and player responses. Both voice override tails reviewed with their preceding fragments.",
    "Ultron four repair states retain initial skepticism, matching precursor signatures, one missing part and incompatibility with human/allied minds. Existing locked names remain unchanged.",
    "Rosy Sphere 5 cm, Aqua Helix Mohs-13 and one meter, Clear Spindle 18-22 C, Mycon .5-3.5 m and egg over 25 m preserved.",
    "Hawkins hesitation and inexperienced speech preserved separately from formal scientist report register; hostile creature danger and destruction-code contact sequence unchanged.",
    "Progress advice retains knowledge gates, need for bomb amplification and removal of guards. Original suggested thruster/crew quantities are retained even where code thresholds differ.",
    "At least 50 crew, possible 200 crew, 50/150 fuel, one lander and one dynamo remain recommendations without invented requirements.",
    "Player questions retain their own polite voice and dynamic ship-name slots; no hardcoded player or ship name introduced."
  ],
